  m_text: '<size=70%><color=#9A6A2E><b>AUDIO 401</b></color></size>

    <b>Vasco da Gama</b>

    <size=74%>Reached Calicut in May 1498

    <i>Portrait, oil on panel, c. 1525</i>

    Museu Nacional de Arte Antiga, Lisbon</size>

    <size=70%><line-height=110%>

    The Portuguese navigator reached Calicut on the Malabar coast in May 1498, opening a sea route from Europe to India around Africa. Portugal soon set up forts and trading posts, and from 1510 ruled Goa, which remained Portuguese until 1961.</size>

    <size=50%><color=#8A8A8A>Photo: Unknown master of the Portuguese School.. / Public domain / Wikimedia Commons</color></size>'
