  mapSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 1634ca45fb36b4c709a0112b36eaea91, type: 3}
  wingId: W4
  sectionTitle: Colonial India
  period: "1498 \u2013 1885"
  questions:
  - text: Which port did Vasco da Gama reach in 1498?
    options:
    - Goa
    - Calicut
    - Surat
    - Cochin
    answer: 1
    why: Vasco da Gama sailed round Africa and reached Calicut in 1498.
  - text: Who defeated Siraj-ud-Daula at the Battle of Plassey in 1757?
    options:
    - Robert Clive
    - Lord Wellesley
    - Lord Dalhousie
    - Warren Hastings
    answer: 0
    why: Robert Clive won at Plassey, helped by Mir Jafar's betrayal.
  - text: Who introduced the Permanent Settlement in Bengal in 1793?
    options:
    - Thomas Munro
    - Cornwallis
    - Holt Mackenzie
    - Macaulay
    answer: 1
    why: Cornwallis introduced the Permanent Settlement in 1793.
  - text: Where did the Revolt of 1857 begin on 10 May 1857?
    options:
    - Delhi
    - Kanpur
    - Meerut
    - Lucknow
    answer: 2
    why: The revolt began at Meerut on 10 May 1857.
  - text: Who founded the Brahmo Samaj in 1828?
    options:
    - Swami Dayananda Saraswati
    - Raja Rammohan Roy
    - Keshab Chandra Sen
    - M. G. Ranade
    answer: 1
    why: Raja Rammohan Roy founded the Brahmo Samaj in 1828.
  - text: Between which two places did India's first passenger train run in 1853?
    options:
    - Calcutta and Hooghly
    - Madras and Arcot
    - Bombay and Thane
    - Delhi and Agra
    answer: 2
    why: The first passenger train ran from Bombay to Thane on 16 April 1853.
  entries:
  - year: 1498
    label: Reached Calicut in May 1498
    title: Vasco da Gama
    credit: 'Photo: Unknown master of the Portuguese School.. / Public domain / Wikimedia Commons'
    target: {fileID: 1812127127}
