      m_Calls: []
  m_text: '<size=70%><color=#9A6A2E><b>AUDIO 403</b></color></size>

    <b>Tipu''s Tiger</b>

    <size=74%>c. 1795

    <i>Painted wood with a mechanical organ</i>

    Victoria and Albert Museum, London</size>

    <size=70%><line-height=110%>

    Made for Tipu Sultan, ruler of Mysore, this life-size wooden tiger mauls a European soldier. Turning a handle works an organ inside that makes the tiger growl and the man wail. Tipu fought four wars against the East India Company; after he died defending Srirangapatna in 1799, the tiger was taken to London.</size>

    <size=50%><color=#8A8A8A>Photo: Sourabh.biswas003 / CC BY-SA 4.0 / Wikimedia Commons</color></size>'
